     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of about 850 to 1,000 mg. At this level the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis goes up, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), the usual maximum\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily**\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, split into divided doses\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily as written, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
